        "original_id": "45368c4f-35cf-590c-b6ed-d5c63615dbfc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Daragh O'Malley, Bob Hoskins, Helen Mirren, Sean Bean, Assumpta Serna, Martin Glyn Murray\n- Works: The Long Good Friday, Withnail and I, Tales of the Unexpected, Waking the Dead, Wire in the Blood, Silent Witness, Vera, Longitude, Cleopatra, The Magnificent Seven, Vendetta, Camelot, Shaughnessy, Sharpe's Rifles, Families, The Bill, Sharpe, Aristocrats, Enigma, Enemy at the Gates, Captain Corelli's Mandolin, Made in Estonia, Heartbeat\n- Organizations: ITV, ABC, CBS\n- Places: Helsingør, Denmark\n- Topics: British film, television acting\n\nFacts:\n- Martin Glyn Murray was born on 1 February 1966 in Helsingør, Denmark.\n- Martin Glyn Murray is a Danish-born British actor.\n- Daragh O'Malley first appeared in roles in the films The Long Good Friday and Withnail and I.\n- The Long Good Friday is a British gangster film starring Bob Hoskins and Helen Mirren.\n- In 1993, Sharpe's Rifles was shown on ITV and starred Sean Bean, Daragh O'Malley, and Assumpta Serna.\n- Daragh O'Malley had leading guest roles in the television series Tales of the Unexpected, Waking the Dead, Wire in the Blood, Silent Witness, and Vera.\n- Daragh O'Malley also appeared in Longitude, Cleopatra for ABC, The Magnificent Seven for CBS, and the US television films Vendetta, Camelot, and Shaughnessy.\n- Martin Glyn Murray played Mark Thompson in Families and also appeared in The Bill, Sharpe, Aristocrats, Enigma, Enemy at the Gates, Captain Corelli's Mandolin, Made in Estonia, and Heartbeat.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
